1
00:00:05,175 --> 00:00:07,725
Last time, we put six things in a box.

2
00:00:07,935 --> 00:00:10,785
The robot moved, but it is a non-living thing.

3
00:00:10,985 --> 00:00:14,015
The green bean stayed still, but it is a living thing.

4
00:00:14,225 --> 00:00:15,885
So what are the real clues?

5
00:00:16,550 --> 00:00:17,760
Not how it looks.

6
00:00:17,990 --> 00:00:19,250
Not whether it moves.

7
00:00:19,480 --> 00:00:20,650
Ask two things.

8
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:21,880
What does it need?

9
00:00:22,170 --> 00:00:23,220
What can it do?

10
00:00:23,719 --> 00:00:26,299
Living things need water, food and air.

11
00:00:26,529 --> 00:00:29,949
Living things grow, respond to changes and reproduce.

12
00:00:30,189 --> 00:00:32,629
You will test these in the next two episodes.

13
00:00:33,755 --> 00:00:35,155
Does it move?

14
00:00:35,405 --> 00:00:36,805
That's NOT the clue!

15
00:00:37,055 --> 00:00:38,455
What does it NEED?

16
00:00:38,705 --> 00:00:40,105
What can it DO?

17
00:00:41,635 --> 00:00:42,515
Day ten.

18
00:00:42,735 --> 00:00:46,975
Time to sort all six into two groups: living things and non-living

19
00:00:46,725 --> 00:00:47,415
things.

20
00:00:47,635 --> 00:00:49,105
Momo, you go first.

21
00:00:49,763 --> 00:00:50,473
Squish...

22
00:00:50,823 --> 00:00:51,493
squish...

23
00:00:51,803 --> 00:00:52,903
knock, knock.

24
00:00:52,983 --> 00:00:53,803
Done!

25
00:00:54,237 --> 00:00:55,707
Something is not right.

26
00:00:55,917 --> 00:00:58,017
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

27
00:00:58,237 --> 00:00:59,147
Hold on!

28
00:01:04,654 --> 00:01:05,764
Arms crossed?

29
00:01:05,984 --> 00:01:07,104
One finger up!

30
00:01:07,344 --> 00:01:08,014
Look.

31
00:01:08,264 --> 00:01:10,434
The teddy bear is sitting with the mealworm.

32
00:01:10,674 --> 00:01:12,704
Momo sorted by soft and hard.

33
00:01:12,843 --> 00:01:14,563
I wanted to know how they feel!

34
00:01:14,713 --> 00:01:15,653
Good sort.

35
00:01:15,783 --> 00:01:17,013
Wrong question.

36
00:01:17,593 --> 00:01:19,613
Momo did put things into groups.

37
00:01:19,853 --> 00:01:21,233
Alike things together.

38
00:01:21,473 --> 00:01:22,983
Different things apart.

39
00:01:23,412 --> 00:01:28,332
Classification is the grouping of things based on their similarities and differences.

40
00:01:32,772 --> 00:01:34,562
You can choose soft or hard.

41
00:01:34,772 --> 00:01:37,312
But our question is living or non-living.

42
00:01:37,532 --> 00:01:39,202
So we use the real clues.

43
00:01:39,422 --> 00:01:40,902
Has anyone done that?

44
00:01:42,674 --> 00:01:44,364
My homework from Day one.

45
00:01:44,564 --> 00:01:46,954
I fixed the green bean after Round two.

46
00:01:47,077 --> 00:01:47,957
Showdown!

47
00:01:48,197 --> 00:01:49,287
Double points.

48
00:01:49,497 --> 00:01:51,557
Pip made a table with two columns.

49
00:01:51,777 --> 00:01:53,857
One thing is still in the wrong column.

50
00:01:56,485 --> 00:01:58,535
Is it one, the wind-up robot?

51
00:01:58,765 --> 00:01:59,835
Two, the plant?

52
00:02:00,055 --> 00:02:01,315
Or three, the pebble?

53
00:02:01,555 --> 00:02:02,955
Show me with your fingers.

54
00:02:09,427 --> 00:02:10,377
Locked in!

55
00:02:10,507 --> 00:02:11,147
Two!

56
00:02:11,267 --> 00:02:12,517
We water that plant.

57
00:02:12,557 --> 00:02:13,657
It needs water.

58
00:02:13,710 --> 00:02:14,500
Two!

59
00:02:14,560 --> 00:02:15,930
I saw a new leaf.

60
00:02:15,981 --> 00:02:18,011
But it never moved out of its pot!

61
00:02:18,588 --> 00:02:21,298
Watch the plant, from day one to day fourteen.

62
00:02:21,538 --> 00:02:22,958
It stays in its pot.

63
00:02:23,158 --> 00:02:24,518
But it has a new leaf.

64
00:02:24,728 --> 00:02:26,978
And it grows towards the light from the window.

65
00:02:27,188 --> 00:02:28,958
The plant is a living thing.

66
00:02:30,299 --> 00:02:30,969
Fixed!

67
00:02:30,719 --> 00:02:33,279
A plant stays in one place.

68
00:02:33,429 --> 00:02:35,179
But it is a living thing.

69
00:02:35,301 --> 00:02:36,291
Two fingers?

70
00:02:36,511 --> 00:02:38,391
Put up two more on your score hand!

71
00:02:38,964 --> 00:02:40,334
Pip used a table.

72
00:02:40,534 --> 00:02:43,264
The same two groups can be shown in other ways too.

73
00:02:43,610 --> 00:02:48,340
We can present our classification using pictures, a table, and a graphic

74
00:02:48,090 --> 00:02:49,060
organiser.

75
00:02:54,682 --> 00:02:55,632
Day thirty.

76
00:02:55,862 --> 00:02:57,202
What is under the cloth?

77
00:02:59,517 --> 00:03:01,677
The green bean is a tall plant now.

78
00:03:01,887 --> 00:03:03,287
The mealworm is bigger.

79
00:03:03,507 --> 00:03:05,097
The plant has new leaves.

80
00:03:05,327 --> 00:03:07,767
And the teddy bear, the robot and the pebble?

81
00:03:08,007 --> 00:03:09,347
Exactly the same.

82
00:03:10,143 --> 00:03:11,413
Three living things.

83
00:03:11,623 --> 00:03:13,093
Three non-living things.

84
00:03:13,253 --> 00:03:14,653
Does it move?

85
00:03:14,903 --> 00:03:16,303
That's NOT the clue!

86
00:03:16,553 --> 00:03:17,953
What does it NEED?

87
00:03:18,203 --> 00:03:19,603
What can it DO?

88
00:03:20,808 --> 00:03:22,198
Show me your score hand!

89
00:03:22,428 --> 00:03:23,438
More than two?

90
00:03:23,668 --> 00:03:24,948
You beat the Buddies.

91
00:03:25,168 --> 00:03:26,228
Three fingers?

92
00:03:26,448 --> 00:03:27,448
High five!

93
00:03:27,945 --> 00:03:29,545
Did you spot the cicak?

94
00:03:29,765 --> 00:03:32,105
It was on the window frame on day fourteen.

95
00:03:32,325 --> 00:03:34,415
Is a cicak living or non-living?

96
00:03:34,625 --> 00:03:35,905
Tell someone at home.

97
00:03:37,570 --> 00:03:38,380
Oh no.

98
00:03:38,560 --> 00:03:39,650
Is it sad?

99
00:03:39,780 --> 00:03:41,490
A drooping plant isn't sad.

100
00:03:41,710 --> 00:03:42,730
What does it need?

101
00:03:42,990 --> 00:03:44,880
Lock in your answer for next time.

102
00:03:47,962 --> 00:03:48,872
Now you know!
